  "body": "Found while reviewing PR 1578 (the STEP face-evaluation cap).\n\nWhat happens: the 150 M evaluation cap is per face, per tessellation pass. A hostile or broken STEP file with many runaway faces therefore costs roughly (runaway faces) x 10-15 s divided by the core count before the import is refused. Edge-curve divisions are not metered at all (issue 1545).\n\nWanted: a cumulative evaluation budget for each tessellation pass. Once the summed trips pass a few caps, the pass stops and the import is refused by name. Edge-curve divisions count against the same budget.\n\nSafety: the importer reads untrusted files; a refusal must stay a clean named error, never a hang or a crash, and a healthy model must import exactly as before.\n\nDone means: a hostile many-face fixture is refused within a bounded time that does not grow with its face count; a test pins the refusal; tests show healthy imports are unchanged.\n\nPart of #1568 and #1546. Relates to #1545.\n",
